Z||000000||Rodney||07-24-2001||08:33 AM||||I just got some V-6 under manifold vacuum line sets back from the power coater. They are a semi-gloss black and look very close to the OEM black plastic. The powder coating should make these last forever. The price is $108 but I have a few sets for an introductory price of $99. Not on my web page yet. <P>Rodney Dickman <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||btoth||07-24-2001||07:12 PM||||I got a set of the originals for Christmas last year and they were great!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000002||Howard_Sacks||07-25-2001||10:49 PM||||I installed the lines on my 87.  They are great. I painted mine with red engine paint, but the new powder coating option would be choice. It was a surprisingly quick install, but make sure you have a new gasket set if you're taking the intake off.<P> After the install of the lines and a new egr tube, I passed NJ inspection and was really far under the limit. <P>My numbers were:<P>Reading  / Standard<BR>NOx 157  /   1378<BR>HC   33  /   180<BR>CO% .23  /   1.01<BR>||||reg||1
